# Object.defineProperty(Math, "k1", { value: 7 }) and nine more: which of them the scan says lay a text, a number or a boolean that is written.
# Yes: 7, "t", true, 1.5. No: null and undefined (no text, number or boolean), a function, a value beside a getter (the call throws), a value that is stored over with a function, one of two values.
# If the scan said yes of one of the last six, a function could be laid on a built-in under the word "a number": Bun's test/aot/engine-tests/link/built-in-that-native-code-hands-to-the-library-is-let-go-where-a-function-is-defined-on-it.ir.
